   "advances_plan": "The Valeyard doubles every Villainous Choice and adds a vote; nonlegendary copies add more.",
   "honest_note": "Commander-native but narrow: two static modifiers, no body-based engine, and no Spellbook combos; the source asserts no infinite (decisions L76). Copies stack additively, not exponentially (L74). The source rejected Prisoner's Dilemma and Seize the Spotlight because 'choose' isn't 'vote' (CR 701.38c). The deck's power comes from its staples more than the commander; expect low Bracket 4."
